 * Scope: boundary-only. No cadence, calibration, airflow, creep, commit
   or storage default changes; the ordinary fast path is untouched.
+
+### Completed wind records after a water event
+
+The forcing record keeps its usual local zero origin. When an external
+scheduler starts a later wind event at an absolute native time, advance each
+block at `origin + local_start` through `origin + local_end`, retain the actual
+native physical clock and cohort timestamps, and apply the native record-loop
+terminal cursor bookkeeping only after the last block is consumed. Then call:
+
+```python
+result = finalize_wind_event(state, scheduler_config, completed_wind_record,
+                             record_origin_s=wind_event_absolute_start_s)
+```
+
+The finalizer compares the unchanged physical end clock with
+`record_origin_s + completed_wind_record.total_duration_s()` using its existing
+completion tolerance. The default origin is zero for existing callers. A bad
+origin, incomplete cursor or mismatched final wind still blocks handoff.
+The origin changes only completed-record bookkeeping; deposition still uses the
+actual event-end physical time and original cohort trajectories. It adds no
+elapsed interval and no artificial forcing prefix. Retain the returned bed,
+ledger and availability and count returned export once, as for a zero-origin event.
